summary:
  Every line for the park file is appended whether or not the file could
  be started.

history:
  That is how it was, and with a runtime folder it made no difference.
  Without one the opening line was skipped and the appends were not: their
  path then begins at the root, /onair_park_7.sh. An ordinary user's shell
  fails there once per speaker and goes on. A shell with the right to
  write there leaves the room's levels in a file nothing will ever read
  back. The appends wait for the flag the opening line sets.

target:
  package/contents/ui/CalibLogic.js

find:
      return " [ -n \"$pk\" ] && printf " + printfArgs + " >> " + parkFile + ";";

replace:
      return " printf " + printfArgs + " >> " + parkFile + ";";

expect:
  Killed by tests/test_calibrate_cancel.py::test_a_runtime_folder_that_is_not_there_costs_the_park_file_and_not_the_levels.
  Line-neutral.
